Production last-write tracking: store `last_write_ts` or `write_lsn` keyed by `user_id` in a centralized cache such as Redis (or the primary itself) so every app instance and device sees the same gate — browser/session-only metadata fails when the user refreshes from another phone. A fixed 60s primary-read window is simple and matches chapter guidance for recent self-reads; LSN wait (`replay_lsn >= write_lsn`) is tighter when you want to return to the replica as soon as it catches up rather than pinning to the primary for a full minute. Monitor `pg_stat_replication.replay_lag` and do not pretend async replication is synchronous.

Comment: AWS RDS Aurora custom writer endpoint + reader endpoint, or a Django database router that forces `using='default'` for recent self-profile reads, is the usual app-layer pattern.
